1. Research Use Only / Not for Clinical Use
--------------------------------------------------------------------

VFDistiller is a bioinformatics research and teaching tool for the
processing, conversion and annotation of genetic variant files (VCF,
gVCF, 23andMe raw format, FASTA). It is explicitly:

  * NOT a CE-marked in-vitro diagnostic medical device (IVD) within
    the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2017/746 (IVDR).
  * NOT certified by BfArM, a notified body or any other regulator.
  * NOT intended for clinical diagnosis, prognosis, therapeutic
    decision-making, or the interpretation of clinical test results
    (including in the consumer-genomics context).
  * NOT a medical opinion, diagnosis or recommendation.

The ClinSig values (from ClinVar), variant-impact predictions (from
Ensembl VEP, AlphaGenome) and allele-frequency annotations (from
gnomAD, ALFA, TOPMed) that VFDistiller displays are database
annotations reproduced from third-party research sources. They are
for scientific orientation only and must not be used as a basis for
clinical decisions.

Any person using VFDistiller to interpret real human genetic data must
consult qualified human-genetics professionals.

